"sevillad@gmail.com" <sevillad@gmail.com> wrote:
>Maybe I lost something for killing a fellow human, even i f
>it was not peaceful any more... I don't have any means of
>enlightenment so I can't find out directly for now.

A lawful or neutral character who kills a monster that is all three of:
a) Human
b) generated as peaceful by default (e.g. watchmen, aligned priests,
   vault guards)
c) actually generated as peaceful (a "renegade priest" on the astral
   plane, or the army of priests of Moloch in the Sanctum, are generated
   as hostile).
is guilty of murder in-game, which incurs a two-point Luck penalty and
removes intrinsic telepathy and (IIRC) any divinely bestowed protection.
It does not remove other divinely bestowed intrinsic abilities.

Chaotic characters are not subject to these special penalties for
killing peaceful humans.
